WEBVTT

00:03.920 --> 00:07.320
Okay, so now what else you can do with the structure of your database?

00:07.320 --> 00:12.920
If you have already a table, what you can do, you can go and edit and change the definition of the

00:12.920 --> 00:13.400
table.

00:13.400 --> 00:16.000
So for example, let's say I would like to add a new column.

00:16.000 --> 00:19.240
In order to do that we can use the command alter.

00:19.280 --> 00:24.800
Alter means you want to edit the definition of your table and you want to change it, like adding new

00:24.800 --> 00:29.200
column, or maybe changing the data type and anything in the definition of the table.

00:29.200 --> 00:33.160
So the alter command, you can use it in order to change the definition of your table.

00:33.160 --> 00:36.080
And now let's go back to SQL and try to change something.

00:36.120 --> 00:36.400
All right.

00:36.440 --> 00:40.800
Now the task says add a new column called email to the persons table.

00:40.800 --> 00:42.320
So it is very simple what you can do.

00:42.320 --> 00:44.600
We can use the alter table command.

00:44.600 --> 00:46.480
So we are not creating new table.

00:46.480 --> 00:49.240
We want to edit already existing table.

00:49.240 --> 00:50.920
So which table we want to modify.

00:50.920 --> 00:52.080
It's going to be the persons.

00:52.080 --> 00:55.480
So we are telling SQL we want to change something in the table persons.

00:55.480 --> 00:58.000
And of course we have to tell SQL what we want to change.

00:58.040 --> 00:59.360
Are we removing the column.

00:59.360 --> 01:00.600
Are we adding column.

01:00.600 --> 01:02.680
And this scenario we want to add a new column.

01:02.680 --> 01:05.560
So let's go and add the email information.

01:05.560 --> 01:07.120
So this is the column name.

01:07.120 --> 01:12.160
And as you are creating a table, you have to define the column name, the data type and the constraint.

01:12.200 --> 01:15.760
So now for the emails you can have like characters numbers, special characters.

01:15.760 --> 01:17.280
So we're going to go with the Varchar.

01:18.080 --> 01:20.400
And about the length it's going to be let's say 50.

01:20.440 --> 01:22.960
And I'm going to say each person has to have an email.

01:22.960 --> 01:24.640
So it's going to be not null.

01:24.880 --> 01:27.680
So with that we are adding completely a new column.

01:27.680 --> 01:28.640
So that's it.

01:28.640 --> 01:30.000
Let's go and execute it.

01:30.040 --> 01:31.800
Now again this is not a query.

01:31.800 --> 01:33.360
This is a DDL command.

01:33.360 --> 01:35.320
And in the output we will not get data.

01:35.320 --> 01:37.920
We will get the message whether everything went correctly.

01:37.920 --> 01:41.760
So it says command completed successfully at the time when this is completed.

01:41.760 --> 01:45.760
Now we can go and do a simple query just to have a check to the table.

01:45.760 --> 01:48.360
So and now you can see we have our columns.

01:48.360 --> 01:50.760
And at the end we have a new column called emails.

01:50.760 --> 01:51.920
This is very important.

01:51.920 --> 01:55.840
If you are adding new column it's going to be always at the end of the table.

01:55.880 --> 01:59.880
But now you might say, you know what, I would like to have the email like something in the middle,

01:59.920 --> 02:01.400
maybe after the person name.

02:01.400 --> 02:06.960
Well, in order to do that, you have completely to delete and drop the table and create it from scratch

02:07.000 --> 02:11.200
using create command, which is might be bad if you have data inside the table.

02:11.200 --> 02:15.950
So if you are, find by adding your new column at the end, you can use the alter table, but if you

02:15.950 --> 02:20.430
say I would like it in the middle, then sadly you have to go and drop everything and start from the

02:20.430 --> 02:20.910
scratch.

02:20.950 --> 02:25.750
Okay, so now let's have another task and it says remove the column phone from the persons table.

02:25.750 --> 02:27.350
So now we're going to do exactly the opposite.

02:27.350 --> 02:31.190
We're going to go remove it completely with its data from the table.

02:31.190 --> 02:33.710
So we can still say alter table persons.

02:33.710 --> 02:37.270
We are saying we want to edit the definition of the table persons.

02:37.310 --> 02:41.270
And now instead of adding we will be dropping a column.

02:41.550 --> 02:45.670
And then after that we have to specify as well the column name going to be the phone.

02:45.670 --> 02:49.830
But we don't have to mention again the data type and the constraint.

02:49.830 --> 02:52.990
And that's because the database already knows those informations.

02:52.990 --> 02:54.270
So we need those informations.

02:54.270 --> 02:57.350
If you are creating something new that's why we can get rid of that.

02:57.350 --> 03:00.510
We just need the column name and the database is going to do the rest.

03:00.510 --> 03:02.630
So let's go and do that.

03:02.670 --> 03:04.190
Now you can see successful.

03:04.230 --> 03:06.350
And now let's go and check our table.

03:06.390 --> 03:09.550
And now as you can see we have the ID person name birth date email.

03:09.550 --> 03:11.110
And we don't have the column phone.

03:11.150 --> 03:11.750
Be careful.

03:11.750 --> 03:16.310
If you are deleting a column you will be losing as well all the data inside this column.

03:16.310 --> 03:17.990
So as you can see this is very simple.

03:17.990 --> 03:22.870
This is how we can edit the definition of our table by adding and remove columns.
